      <title>Shader Compiler Optimisation Strategies</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>X.org</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Different GPUs have different architectures and thus require different shader compiler optimisations for more optimal performance.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This talk explains some of the differences between both AMD, Nvidia and Intel GPUs and will present some compiler algorithms to optimise shaders accordingly.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2991">Jerome Glisse</person>
      </persons>
